 Did early audiences for The Odyssey find any parts of it funny?  Would any bits of it be played for laughs in performance? 

Contemporary performance, even when deeply serious, often has comic relief bits (Shakespeare’s porters and gravediggers etc.) but maybe not Homer?

The thing we should really be talking about in regards to The Odyssey is ticket scalpers. 

The show is completely sold out in 70mm IMAX until the end of its run at the only theatre in NYC to show it in that format. That seems very much off. Protections are needed against mass buys.
@mayor.nyc.gov

